<title>SOUTH KOREA: Samsung to export celullar handsets to HK.</title>
<headline>Samsung to export celullar handsets to HK.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Samsung Electronics Co said on Tuesday it had signed a contract with Hutchison Telecom Hong Kong to export 20,000 digital celullar telephone handsets adopting the code-division multiple access (CDMA) format.</p>
<p>The flagship unit of Samsung Group said it was also close to signing a deal with the Hong Kong firm, a unit of Hutchison Whampoa Ltd, for another 20,000 sets.</p>
<p>The two deals are expected to amount to about $20 million, a spokesman for Samsung said.</p>
<p>Delivery is due for the first quarter of 1997, he said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
